meta {
  name: IMFS
}

docs {
  # IMFS API Collection

  Bruno collection for the **IMFS / MicroFlow** backend (J26-IT-326).

  ## What this is
  Shared API tests for the Node + Prisma backend under `/backend`.
  Use this instead of ad-hoc Postman setups so the whole team hits the same endpoints.

  ## Base URL
  Local default: `{{baseUrl}}` → `http://localhost:4000`

  1. Start backend: `cd backend` → `npm run dev`
  2. In Bruno, select environment **Local**
  3. Run **00 Health → Health** then **Health DB**

  ## Architecture (short)
  - **Central DB** — institutions, users, roles, tenant routing
  - **Tenant DB** — one database per MFI (loans, risk, EWS, ledger, agents)
  - Auth target: **JWT + RBAC** (6 roles) — not fully wired yet

  ## Folder guide
  | Folder | Owner / purpose |
  |--------|-----------------|
  | `00 Health` | Connectivity checks (everyone) |
  | `01 Auth` | Login, signup, JWT (M4) |
  | `02 Central` | Institutions, users, routing (M4) |
  | `03 Onboarding` | Provision tenant DB (M4) |
  | `10 M1 Risk` | `/assess-risk`, decisions (M1) |
  | `20 M2 Finance` | Ledger, KPIs, MDI (M2) |
  | `30 M3 Loans` | Applications, collections, EWS (M3) |
  | `40 M4 Agents` | Graduated Trust / tier approvals (M4) |

  ## Team rules
  - Add requests under the correct module folder
  - Prefer `{{baseUrl}}` — never hardcode localhost in every request
  - Do not commit secrets; use Bruno env vars / `.env` on the machine
  - Keep request names clear: `GET Health`, `POST Assess Risk`, etc.

  ## Docs
  - Backend overview: `docs/BACKEND_GUIDE.md`
  - Local Postgres setup: `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md`
}

auth {
  mode: none
}
